uence, invalid chars). Record warnings.\n   - Parse CDS= start-end from header if present. Validate: integer, start <= end, start >= 1, end <= len(seq), length % 3 == 0. Flag issues.\n2. Parse inputs/primer_candidates.csv with csv.DictReader. Validate columns and DNA letters.\n3. For each pair × each transcript:\n   - Find all exact matches of forward on sense strand.\n   - Find all exact matches of revcomp(reverse) on sense strand.\n   - Also compute best near-match (min Hamming mismatches over windows of primer length) for reporting when there's no exact match.\n   - Form amplicons for fwd_start < rev_end (and fwd_end < rev_start, i.e., non-overlapping, forward upstream): amplicon = fwd_start..rev_end, length = rev_end - fwd_start + 1.\n   - Handle multiple matches: if multiple, report all; transcripts_matched if ≥1 amplicon.\n4. CDS compatibility: amplicon within [cds_start, cds_end] (and metadata valid); otherwise no; if metadata invalid → no with reason \"cds metadata inconsistent\".\n5. Determine status per pair:\n   - expected_transcript not in FASTA → \"expected_transcript_missing\".\n   - No amplicon on any transcript → \"no_amplicon\".\n   - Amplicon found: on expected transcript? If on expected and length == expected_product_bp and CDS compatible and metadata consistent → \"ok\". If on expected but length differs → \"length_mismatch\". Amplicon only on non-expected → \"off_target\". Amplicon on expected plus others → note.\n6. Write CSV with csv.writer (QUOTE_MINIMAL).\n7. Emit report.md with: inputs summary, transcript table with metadata validation results, per-pair audit details, warnings/inconsistencies section, methods.\n\nEdge details:\n- Reverse-complement function.\n- Best near-match: slide window of primer length over transcript, count mismatches; record min; report for primers without exact match (e.g., p01 reverse on TX_ALT: min mismatches = 2 at position 83; p02 reverse revcomp on TX_CAN: 2 at position 83; p03: min mismatches for poly-A is aro