does not\").\n4. CDS: f\"{tx} CDS={start}-{end} exceeds sequence length {len} (inconsistent metadata, not repaired); amplicon not contained in annotated CDS\" → cds_compatible no.\n5. For p03: \"homopolymer primers (20A/20T) with no exact match in any supplied transcript\".\n6. If expected product bp > expected transcript length: \"expected product 120 bp exceeds transcript length 102 nt (impossible)\".\n\nAlso global warnings list for the report: from FASTA parsing (CDS issues), from primer parsing, plus cross-check of expected product size vs transcript length for each pair.\n\nOK let me structure the report generation. Write a function build_report(...) producing Markdown.\n\nAlso, console output: print the CSV table and warnings.\n\nNow, \"date\" in the report: use datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\"). Good (2026-08-27).\n\nLet me also verify the best_near_match for p01 reverse on TX_ALT once more: rev_rc = GACCTGACTGACCTGAATGA; window 83-102 of alt = GACCTGACTGACCTGAATAG → mismatches at positions 19, 20 of window → mm=2 at 1-based position 83. Could there be a better window with fewer mismatches somewhere else? Windows inside the repeat: e.g., starting at 84: \"ACCTGACTGACCTGAATAG?\" only 19 nt remaining — not full. Start 82: positions 82-101 = \"TGACCTGACTGACCTGAATA\" vs motif \"GACCTGACTGACCTGAATGA\": compare: T vs G mm, G vs A mm, A vs C mm, C vs C ok, C vs T mm, T vs G mm, G vs A mm, A vs C mm, C vs T mm, T vs G mm... lots. So best is 2 at position 83. Good.\n\nFor p03: min mismatches for 20A window: need max A-count in any 20-window of S_can. Sequence A's: positions: from ATGG (A at 1), U units: A's at positions 4, 9, 13, 18, 19 within U. Roughly 5 A's per 19 nt → max in 20-window probably 6-7 → mismatches ~13-14. Script computes.\n\nOK let me write it all. Also handle CRLF in inputs (Windows). open with newline handling; strip.\n\nOne more thought: should analysis.py also validate that the FASTA IDs are unique? Add duplicate-ID check → warning. Not