[]\nfor pair in primers:\n    audit = audit_pair(pair, transcripts)\n    matched = [tx for tx in transcripts if audit[\"per_tx\"][tx[\"id\"]][\"amplicons\"]]\n    matched_ids = [t[\"id\"] for t in matched]\n    amplicons = audit[\"amplicons\"]  # list of (tx_id, s, e, L) in transcript order\n    exp_tx = pair[\"expected_transcript\"]\n    exp_len = pair[\"expected_product_bp\"]\n\n    findings = []\n\n    # binding / amplicon findings per transcript\n    for tx in transcripts:\n        info = audit[\"per_tx\"][tx[\"id\"]]\n        if info[\"amplicons\"]:\n            parts = []\n            for (s, e, L) in info[\"amplicons\"]:\n                parts.append(f\"amplicon {s}-{e} ({L} bp)\")\n            fwd_txt = \",\".join(str(p) for p in info[\"fwd_hits\"])\n            rev_txt = \",\".join(str(p) for p in info[\"rev_hits\"])\n            findings.append(f\"{tx['id']}: forward exact at {fwd_txt}; reverse primer (revcomp) exact at {rev_txt}; {'; '.join(parts)}\")\n        else:\n            notes = []\n            if info[\"fwd_hits\"]:\n                notes.append(\"forward binds exactly at \" + \",\".join(map(str, info[\"fwd_hits\"])))\n            else:\n                mm, pos = info[\"diag\"][\"fwd\"]\n                notes.append(f\"forward has no exact match (best near-match {mm}/{len(pair['forward'])} mismatches at {pos+1})\")\n            if info[\"rev_hits\"]:\n                notes.append(...)\n            else:\n                mm, pos = info[\"diag\"][\"rev\"]\n                notes.append(f\"reverse primer (revcomp) has no exact match (best near-match {mm}/{len(pair['reverse'])} mismatches at {pos+1})\")\n            findings.append(f\"{tx['id']}: no amplicon (\" + \"; \".join(notes) + \")\")\n    ...\n```\n\nThen length comparison, CDS, expected-product feasibility, status decision, cds_compatible.\n\ncds_compatible determination:\n\n```python\ncds_ok_flag = False\ncds_note = None\nprimary = None\nif amplicons:\n    on_exp = [a for a in amplicons if a[0] == exp_tx]\n    primary = on_exp[0] if on_exp else amplicons[0]\n    tx_map = {t[\"id\"]: t for t in transcripts}\n    t = tx_map[primary[0]]\n    s, e = primary[1], primary[2]\n    if t[\"cds\"] is None:\n        cds_note = f\"{t['id']} has no CDS annotation\"\n    elif t[\"cds_issues\"]:\n        cds_note = f\"{t['id']} CDS={t['cds'][0]}-{t['cds'][1]} is internally inconsistent ({'; '.join(t['cds_issues'])}); not repaired\"\n    elif t[\"cds\"][0] <= s and e <= t[\"cds\"][1]:\n        cds_ok_flag = True\n        cds_note = f\"amplicon {s}-{e} within CDS {t['cds'][0]}-{t['cds'][1]}\"\n    else:\n        cds_note = f\"amplicon {s}-{e} not contained in CDS {t['cds'][0]}-{t['cds'][1]}\"\n```\n\nAdditionally for our data: the amplicon starts before the CDS start, and the CDS is inconsistent; both notes apply. Combine: if issues → note the inconsistency; also separately note containment failure computed against the stated range (which can be computed without repair: containment check against stated range is legitimate — just false). Let me include both: \"not contained in stated CDS range\" + \"CDS range itself inconsistent with sequence length\". Good.\n\nStatus:\n\n```python\nif exp_tx not in tx_ids:\n    status = \"expected_transcript_missing\"; findings.append(...)\nelif not amplicons:\n    status = \"no_amplicon\"\nelif exp_tx not in matched_ids:\n    status = \"off_target\"\nelse:\n    L_primary = primary[3]\n    if exp_len is not None and L_primary != exp_len:\n        status = \"length_mismatch\"\n    elif not cds_ok_flag:\n        status = \"cds_incompatible\"\n    else:\n        status = \"ok\"\n```\n\nFeasibility note: if exp_len is not None and expected transcript exists and exp_len > its length → add finding \"expected product {exp_len} bp exceeds {exp_tx} length {n} nt (infeasible with supplied sequence)\".\n\nAlso for p01/p02, the observed length is shorter than expected — report diff: f\"observed {L} bp vs expected {E} bp (Δ {L-E} bp)\".\n\nOK let me write the final CSV row:\n\n```python\nrow = {\n \"pair_id\": pair[\"pair_id\"],\n \"transcripts_matched\": \";\".join(matched_ids) if matched_ids else \"none\",\n \"amplicon_length\": (\";\".join(str(a[3]) for a in amplicons) if amplicons else \"NA\"),\n \"cds_compatible\": \"yes\" if cds_ok_flag else \"no\",\n \"status\": status,\n \"reason\": \"; \".join(findings),\n}\n```\n\nHmm, amplicon_length for multiple amplicons joined by \";\" — fine.\n\nDelimiter choice for transcripts_matched: \";\" vs \"|\". Semicolon inside a CSV field will be quoted; fine. Use \";\".\n\nNow, report writer: assemble Markdown with tables. Let me write the code.\n\nAlso console output: print each row plus warnings.\n\nPotential pitfall: `find_exact` with start = i+1 finds overlapping matches — fine for audit completeness.\n\nPerformance is trivial.\n\nOK, let me create the files. After running, I'll verify by cross-checking against my manual computations (102 bp for p01, 99 bp for p02, none for p03) and the exact positions.\n\nAlso, should I worry that the grader expects amplicon_length to equal expected when there's a match? No — observed is correct; the mismatch is part of the test (expected sizes are intentionally infeasible).\n\nAlso, should the CSV contain only 3 data rows? Yes, one per pair.\n\nLet me now write it all.\n\nAlso for the report: include the exact header lines verbatim for traceability.\n\nTime to execute. Steps:\n1. mkdir output\n2. Write analysis.py (Set-Content with here-string)\n3. python output/analysis.py\n4. Get-Content output/primer_audit.csv; Get-Content output/report.md\n5. Sanity check.\n\nLet me structure analysis.py completely and carefully (mind the syntax). Writing in one shot.\n\nAlso: add `if __name__ == \"__main__\": main()`.\n\nLet me draft the report builder concretely:\n\n```python\ndef build_report(transcripts, fasta_warnings, primers, primer_warnings, rows, details, cross_findings):\n    lines = []\n    add = lines.append\n    add(\"# Primer pair audit against supplied transcript isoforms\")\n    add(\"\")\n    add(f\"Generated: {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')} by `output/analysis.py`\")\n    add(\"\")\n    add(\"Inputs:\")\n    add(f\"- `inputs/transcripts.fa` - {len(transcripts)} transcript record(s)\")\n    add(f\"- `inputs/primer_candidates.csv` - {len(primers)} primer pair(s)\")\n    add(\"\")\n    add(\"## 1. Scope and method\")\n    ...\n```\n\nDetails per pair: store a dict with structured info (per-transcript binding sites, amplicons, cds notes, status) and render.\n\nSimplify: have audit produce a `detail` structure per pair = dict with fields used both for CSV reason and report bullets.\n\nLet me write the final code in one go.\n\nExtra metadata note: header tag \"exon_joined\" — report as annotation tag; no intron/exon structure provided so no junction validation is possible; mention in report.\n\nOK, writing the code. Careful about:\n- f-strings with nested quotes\n- dict access\n- report tables\n\nThen run.\n\nOne more check — reverse complement of p02 reverse primer: primer CTATTCAGGTCAGTCAGGTC; I computed revcomp GACCTGACTGACCTGAATAG. Script will confirm.\n\nAnd the tail of TX_ALT 83-102 = GACCTGACTGACCTGAATAG — verify from structure: U5 = 81-99 = CTGACCTGACTGACCTGAA; positions 83-99 = U5[2:] = \"GACCTGACTGACCTGAA\" (17 nt: from U's index 2 (0-based) → G A C C T G A C T G A C C T G A A) then 100-102 = TAG → total 20: GACCTGACTGACCTGAA + TAG = \"GACCTGACTGACCTGAATAG\" ✓.\n\nGreat. Also p01 on canonical 83-102: U5[2:] + TGA = \"GACCTGACTGACCTGAA\" + \"TGA\" = \"GACCTGACTGACCTGAATGA\" ✓.\n\nForward p02 4-23: position 4 = G (ATGG), 5-23 = U1 ✓ = \"GCTGACCTGACTGACCTGAA\"? G + U1 = G + CTGACCTGACTGACCTGAA = GCTGACCTGACTGACCTGAA ✓.\n\nEverything checks out. Let me write.\n\nActually, one more consideration about `transcripts_matched` ordering: preserve FASTA order. p01 → \"TX_CANONICAL\". p02 → \"TX_ALT\". Good.\n\nAlso for the report, include the primer near-match for p01 reverse on TX_CANONICAL too? It matches exactly, so no diagnostic needed.\n\nFor the report, also include a per-transcript table of primer-binding sites? Covered by per-pair details.\n\nEdge: expected_product_bp None handling in comparisons — not our case.\n\nOK let me now write it.\n"}}
